00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
over the years jonah hill has matured  from a comedy staple to a respected  actor with two oscar nominations but  he's also taken a few steps back from  the spotlight  here's why you may not have seen much of  him recently  despite his recent lack of face time  hill has still been busy bulking up his  acting resume  even if you haven't actually seen him  there's a good chance you've heard him  in one of the animated projects he's  lent his voice to  hill's most recent live-action roles  have been confined to the small screen  his last appearance was his cameo as  himself in hbo's curb your enthusiasm in  2020  and he hasn't had a leading role since  starring in netflix's maniac in 2018.  in the time between however hill lent  his voice to two animated sequel films  he reprised his role as snotlout in how  to train your dragon the hidden world  and made another appearance as green  lantern in the lego movie 2  the second part of course voice acting  is nothing new to hell as he first went  behind the microphone for the role of  tommy in the 2008 adaptation  of the dr seuss classic horton hears a  who he's also played a foul-mouthed hot  dog in the notoriously raunchy sausage  party and the super-powered titan  in megamind there is no easter bunny  there is no tooth fairy  and there is no queen of england in 2019  hill had a supporting role in harmony  karine's flick the beach bum  as lewis the bombastic agent of  hedonistic poet moondog played by  matthew mcconaughey  karine known for unsettling movies such  as gummo and spring breakers  is a polarizing director and reviews for  the beach bum certainly reflected that  public reception for the film was mixed  and most critics found it somewhere  between mediocre and middling in his  review for the guardian peter bradshaw  wrote writer director harmony karine  achieves a zen state of unfunny with  this pointless non-comedy  this can only provoke something like awe  that something so awful can still get  made  the beach bum underperformed at the box  office and wasn't exactly in the running  for any  academy awards with so many great films  already on hill's resume  the beach bum doesn't necessarily stand  out as a prime example of his work  so he didn't receive much publicity for  the few scenes in which he appears when  all was said and done however he may be  thankful for that  if you were to ask hill which role he  was the most proud of there's a good  chance he would tell you it was his part  in the 2018 gus  van sant biopic don't worry he won't get  far on foot  hill played donnie green the alcoholics  anonymous sponsor for joaquin phoenix's  john callahan  a man left quadriplegic after a drunk  driving accident who regains his  strength by drawing irreverent cartoons  although hill loved working on the film  and looks back on it as a highlight of  his career he was frustrated with the  lackluster marketing campaign the movie  received he expressed disappointment  with amazon studios for not properly  promoting the film telling gq  it's the best acting i have done or will  ever do but no one saw it  critics generally enjoy don't worry he  won't get far on foot which stands at a  77 percent fresh rating on rotten  tomatoes in her review for the evening  standard critic charlotte o'sullivan  wrote  basically you can't take your eyes off  hell and you get the feeling that  phoenix can't either  that gravitational pull is exactly right  for the story  donnie rearranges john's universe the  path to enlightenment is to know  yourself  how do i know myself forget yourself  if you're a fan of the dc universe you  may remember rumors that hill was slated  to appear in warner brothers newest  iteration of the caped crusader  matt reeves the batman hill was  allegedly lined up to play a villain in  the film opposite robert pattinson  as bruce wayne while warner brothers  never confirmed which villain hill was  in talks to portray  rumor had it that he was being  considered for the role of oswald  cobblepot  otherwise known as the penguin however  hill's talks with the studio  ultimately did not lead to a part in the  film and the news broke that hill was no  longer in consideration for the role  instead the movie has moved along with  colin farrell as the penguin  paul dano as the riddler and zoe  kravitz's catwoman the last of which  hill was almost certainly never  considered to play the batman recently  wrapped filming and is scheduled to be  released in 2022  hill has no intentions of giving up  acting but has been interested in  writing and directing since his  childhood today he's taking on  projects that give him the chance to get  behind the camera hill has experimented  with writing and directing before  he wrote for the short-lived tv series  alan gregory in 2011  and contributed to the storylines for  both jump street movies he has served as  a producer on films like richard jewell  and the documentary beastie boys story  hill has also directed multiple music  videos  including vampire weekend sunflower and  travis scott's wake up in 2018  hill made his childhood dreams come true  when he wrote and directed his own film  the coming-of-age comedy drama mid-90s  the movie tells the story of stevie  a 13 year old with a troubled home life  who finds a sense of brotherhood with a  group of skateboarders in la  mid-90s received positive reviews from  critics and chances seem good that hill  will attempt to direct another film in  the future while such efforts behind the  camera may interfere with acting  opportunities hill seems intent on  branching out  hill has never been shy about his sense  of style and several years ago he  decided that he wanted to start his very  own clothing line before he could even  begin the process however  adidas reached out to him and offered  the opportunity to collaborate on a  collection in an interview discussing  the launch with gq  hill said it was like of course i'm  going to learn from these geniuses and  collaborate with them who wouldn't take  that opportunity  and to get your stuff worn and seen by  more people and also have a great  education  he'll put his personal apparel ideas on  hold with plans to later reply lessons  learned from adidas towards future  efforts as a clothier he explained that  the design process was  time-consuming hill began officially  collaborating with adidas and working on  the line  two years before was released to the  public in 2020  now that he's wrapped up the work on his  adidas collection though he's free to  pursue his dream of starting his own  clothing lot  hill has had multiple unfortunate  interactions with the press that have  left him feeling less than enthused  known to clash with the paparazzi in  public hill makes it no secret when he  thinks someone is being too nosy into  his private life  ever president hill's life has been the  issue of his weight a media  preoccupation that has impacted his  self-confidence  while he hopes that people understand  his worst interactions with the press  don't represent who he really is hill  admits that he's exasperated with public  scrutiny in an instagram post responding  to paparazzi photos of him at the beach  being published in the daily mail  hill wrote i don't think i ever took my  shirt off in a pool until i was in my  mid-30s even in front of family and  friends  probably would have happened sooner if  my childhood insecurities weren't  exacerbated by years of public mockery  about my body by press and interviewers  when you consider the toll that such  statements can have on someone who spent  over a decade in the public  eye it's no wonder that hill prefers to  maintain strong boundaries between his  personal and professional life  hill is an undeniably funny actor having  made audiences laugh for years  often at his own expense but despite  receiving pressure to appear in more  comedies  hill is much pickier about the roles he  accepts today and makes it clear that he  doesn't want to continue  playing the same characters for the rest  of his career hill told indy wire  i love those films but i also think that  if you look back at those films  a lot of what they're showing is major  bro comedy and bro masculinity  hill is open to passing up comedies to  pursue more serious roles he's also on  the lookout for opportunities to work  with female directors  having told the guardian it's insane  that my perspective as an actor has only  been a male's vision  perhaps hill won't be on screen as much  as he used to be simply because he's  being more selective  but his future roles will certainly be  worth keeping an eye on  hill is very close with his family his  sister beanie feldstein has appeared in  films like lady bird and book booksmart  and his brother jordan feldstein managed  to ban maroon 5.  however tragedy struck hill's family in  2017  when jordan unexpectedly passed away  after suffering a pulmonary embolism at  just 40 years old hill was devastated by  his brother's passing and in the  aftermath of jordan's death he preferred  to maintain his privacy rather than  speaking to the press about his loss  however his sister beanie published an  essay in in style titled grief glasses  in which she described her experience of  grief as wearing a pair of glasses that  she couldn't take off  she wrote and these glasses make me see  the world differently than i did before  the colors bleed together more vividly  but they are somehow more than they ever  were before  more visceral more vibrant more present  simultaneously more awe-inspiring and  more aching  hill has appeared in plenty of films  produced by hollywood's most storied  studios but while actors can benefit  from working on tentpole films the  paycheck in publicity comes with a lot  of pressure  as hill continues his pivot to working  on passion projects  and trying his hand at writing and  directing he has increasingly realized  that putting out a film with a big  studio just  isn't always worth it in an interview  with vulture hill said that he now  prefers to work with smaller studios  because he doesn't like to deal with the  expectation to quote make a bajillion  dollars and be so mainstream  that's why he chose to release mid 90s  with a24  a smaller independent studio known for  distributing critically acclaimed flicks  like moonlight and the lighthouse the  way hill sees it  working with a24 gave him the freedom to  depict the story he wanted to tell in  mid-90s without compromising his  artistic vision  if you're looking forward to seeing hill  on screen again you're in luck  he has been hard at work on the upcoming  netflix political satire don't look up  written and directed by adam mckay of  vice and the big short fame the film  features an a-list cast  led by leonardo dicaprio and jennifer  lawrence as a pair of astronomers who  try to warn earth about an  approaching asteroid only to discover  that society is less receptive to their  efforts than they had hoped  hill is reportedly playing the son and  chief of staff of meryl streep's  president of the united states like many  other projects production on the film  was intermittently delayed in 2020  because of covert 19 regulations however  don't look up is currently expected to  get a release in late 2021 and with a  cast that includes plenty of big names  it seems likely to get plenty of major  attention  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

